{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Generic Type.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Generic Type.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"generic type generic type","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Generic Type.md","fileName":"Generic Type.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Generic Type","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-06 20:37\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Front-End Service Design]] [[C Sharp Interfaces Generics and Inheritance]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Front-End Service Design","C Sharp Interfaces Generics and Inheritance","Derived Class","hands-onobject-orientedprogrammingwithc.pdf","aspnetcore3andangular9_3ed.pdf","c80andnetcore30moderncross-platformdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Generic Type.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Generic Type.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"generic type generic type","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Generic Type.md","fileName":"Generic Type.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Generic Type","heading":"Generic Type","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A generic type expresses an operation or structure in terms of a type variable supplied by its user. One interface or base service can therefore work with cities, countries, or another model while preserving the specific return type.\n\nUsing a type parameter is more informative than replacing every value with an unrestricted type. The generic abstraction captures what the operations share and lets a [[Derived Class]] specialize it.\n\nGenerics preserve type safety while reusing a class, struct, interface, or method across multiple types. Compared with storing everything as `object`, a generic parameter avoids routine casts and lets the compiler reject incompatible uses earlier.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Front-End Service Design","C Sharp Int